= Organization =

BITwiki V2 separates independent dimensions of knowledge instead of forcing them into one hierarchy.

== Structural dimensions ==
* '''Namespace''' — system role or page class.
* '''Entity type''' — what kind of thing the page describes.
* '''Domain''' — field or fields of knowledge.
* '''Scope''' — optional contextual boundary when one is real and useful.
* '''Book Matter''' — reusable semantic sections of the content.
* '''Epistemics''' — source, evidence, provenance, status, confidence, uncertainty, and verification.
* '''Relationships''' — semantic links between knowledge objects.

These dimensions are orthogonal. Namespace is not domain; domain is not Book Matter; epistemic status is not a category family.

== Namespace policy ==
Use native MediaWiki namespaces for their real purposes:
* Main — primary public knowledge.
* User / User talk — users and user discussion.
* BITwiki / BITwiki talk — project policy, architecture, governance, standards, and meta documentation.
* Help — editing and usage guidance.
* Template — reusable transclusion and presentation interfaces.
* Module — reusable Lua logic.
* Property — Semantic MediaWiki property definitions.
* Concept — stored semantic queries and computed collections.
* Category — human classification and navigation.
* File — media and file metadata.
* MediaWiki — site interface and system-message content.

Create custom namespaces only when a genuine operational boundary justifies them, such as materially different permissions or behavior.

== Categories ==
Categories should group pages that share meaningful characteristics, especially knowledge domains and useful navigational classes. They should not imitate folders and should not duplicate every semantic property.

== Portals and indexes ==
Portals, indexes, outlines, graphs, and dashboards are generated or curated views over the underlying model. Their purpose is orientation and discovery.

== Historical lesson ==
V1 mixed domains, page types, Book Matter, epistemics, governance, implementation details, and navigation into overlapping category and Main-namespace families. V2 preserves the useful concepts while removing that coupling.

